{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_bdivwl5cl4sxlxia7ttbwvqt5qyusbgwydp26u3ykvfin5dxdpra","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 6 tests pass. The build emits only a `dead_code` warning for the `find` method (a required signature in the interface that the actual implementation doesn't use directly — I implemented packing using a path-based navigator since Rust's borrow checker requires returning the parent root reference).\n\nSummary of the implementation:\n\n- **`Rect::new`** — constructs a `Rect` with default `RectOutInfo`.\n- **`RectPacker::pack`** — sorts rectangles by max-side then min-side (descending) and runs the bin-tree packing loop with optional paging, mirroring the C `rect_pack`.\n- **`BinNode::find`** — recursive search for a free node large enough to fit `(w, h)`.\n- **`BinNode::split`** — marks the node used and creates `down` and `right` children for the leftover space.\n- **`BinNode::grow_right` / `grow_down`** — grow the bin tree to accommodate a rectangle, replicating the C's \"shift current root into a child\" trick.\n- **`BinNode::grow`** — picks the optimal grow direction based on the C heuristics.\n- **Helper `pack_bin_tree`** — iterates rectangles, finding/splitting or growing the tree as needed; tracks `all_fit`, `none_fit`, `next`, and `last` with the same contiguous-prefix semantics as the C version.\n- A path-based navigator (`find_path` + `navigate_mut`/`navigate`) is used internally to satisfy Rust's borrow-checker while preserving the C algorithm's mutation pattern."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":773,"cache_read_input_tokens":37867,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":773,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a90629c5-3652-4a91-a1e9-8af46c3c1cc2","uuid":"c081a3f8-b98